{"name":"Cabaret Charm","hex":"#7c8ea6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabaret","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Live entertainment held in a restaurant or nightclub; the genre of music associated with this form of entertainment, especially in early 20th century Europe.","The nightclub or restaurant where such entertainment is held."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabaret"},{"term":"charm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An object, act or words believed to have magic power (usually carries a positive connotation).","The ability to persuade, delight or arouse admiration."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To seduce, persuade or fascinate someone or something.","To use a magical charm upon; to subdue, control, or summon by incantation or supernatural influence; to ensorcel or exert a magical effect on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cabaret","blocks":[{"text":"Cabaret is a form of theatrical entertainment featuring music, song, dance, recitation, or drama. The performance venue might be a pub, casino, hotel, restaurant, or nightclub with a stage for performances. The audience, often dining or drinking, does not typically dance but usually sits at tables. Performances are usually introduced by a master of ceremonies (M.C.). The entertainment, as performed by an ensemble of actors and according to its European origins, is often oriented towards adult audiences and of a clearly underground nature. In the United States, striptease, burlesque, drag shows, or a solo vocalist with a pianist, as well as the venues which offer this entertainment, are often advertised as cabarets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec%2C_French_-_At_the_Moulin_Rouge-_The_Dance_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/330px-Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec%2C_French_-_At_the_Moulin_Rouge-_The_Dance_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabaret","wikidata":"Q131183"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Caf%C3%A9_des_aveugles.jpg/500px-Caf%C3%A9_des_aveugles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Caf%C3%A9_des_aveugles.jpg/500px-Caf%C3%A9_des_aveugles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Café des Aveugles (\"Café of the Blind\") in the cellars of the Palais-Royal at the beginning of the 19th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaf%C3%A9_des_aveugles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Santiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Santiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Santiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Santiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Santiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Santiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The composer Eric Satie playing the harmonium at Le Chat Noir (1880s)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASantiago_Rusi%C3%B1ol_-_Portrait_of_Erik_Satie_Playing_the_Harmonium_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/